From: Harvi654 <202698022+Harvi654@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wbemdisp: Invoke WMI methods through IDispatch.

AI-assisted (Codex), original code; LGPL-2.1-or-later. Not submitted upstream.

Offline Windows 10 executes method members for METHOD and METHOD |
PROPERTYGET, accepts a missing output or trailing argument, and reports
the provider status and by-reference outputs separately. Wine rejected
the invocation or treated the name as a property. Route positional
method calls through the signature and IWbemServices::ExecMethod, leaving
ordinary property and type-library dispatch on their existing paths.

v2 2026-11-25: no code change. The wbemdisp test moves from tests-first
into the patch and its todo_wine is dropped (all 26 Invoke checks pass
with the patch). Promoted to the series for winum-11.22-3.

